              "width": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 16,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Rmj1b",
                  "name": "aboutTitle",
                  "fill": "$--color-text",
                  "content": "About Anna",
                  "fontFamily": "Playfair Display",
                  "fontSize": 28,
                  "fontWeight": "700"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "TSO7C",
                  "name": "aboutBio",
                  "fill": "$--color-text",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Born and raised in Stockholm, Anna has been sharing her passion for the city's rich history for over a decade. With a Master's in Art History from Stockholm University, she brings academic depth and infectious enthusiasm to every tour.\n\nHer specialty lies in bringing medieval Gamla Stan to life — from the narrow cobblestone alleys to the grand royal chambers. She has an extraordinary ability to weave together the stories of kings, merchants, and everyday Stockholmers into a compelling narrative that makes 700 years of history feel vivid and immediate.\n\nAnna believes that the best tours create genuine connections — between people, places, and the past. Her guests frequently comment on her warmth, humor, and the way she makes everyone feel like they're exploring the city with a knowledgeable friend.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.7,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
